{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to the outage report on ad99c669. The planner deployed approved diagnostic head 09910112 to dap-grow at 06:21 Eastern as version 1312b23c, register mode. At 06:25 the sweep of the saved Grow manifest verified 11 of 11 scopes. The tail from 06:22 to 06:27 holds no scope-index-registration record: no fixed phase refused and no namespace call was rejected.\n\nRoom A's journal shows that the outage lasted about 7 minutes, not one hour. It has no entries from 05:18 to 05:25 Eastern, then one simulator act each minute from 05:25 on. Both failed sweeps ran at 05:18:33 and 05:19:38, within 90 seconds of the fbb6468f deploy. The planner reads this as deploy turnover: the five archive-bound objects still ran 520aa54f code, and that code has no registerKnown method, so the call rejected and the adapter answered not-found. The planner did not sweep again after the turnover, and the earlier report of a lasting outage was wrong.\n\nBuilder: land the approved diagnostic head 09910112 on main, because dap-grow now runs it. Then close ad99c669 with a report that cites this evidence. No repair head is needed. Removal of the temporary observation can follow in a later head. Planner next: enforce on dap-grow per the runbook, with rollback to 1312b23c (register) on any failed row.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}